<title>BELGIUM: Belgium raises women's retirement age to 65-source.</title>
<headline>Belgium raises women's retirement age to 65-source.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian government has decided to raise the women's retirement age to 65 from 60 over a 13-year period as part of its 1997 budget agreement, a government source told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;Retirement age for women will be brought in line with that for men in a 13-year period,&quot; the source said.  </p>
<p>He said this would have little impact on the 1997 budget, but already formed part of a reform of the social security sector that is scheduled for next year.</p>
<p>-- Geert De Clercq, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6813, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
